The appeal must be filed within 45 days from the date a copy of the order is delivered to you. The appellate authority can accept a late appeal if it is satisfied you had sufficient cause [(Rule 25, PDF p. 29)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=29).

Rule 26 sets the form of the appeal [(Rule 26, PDF p. 29)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=29):

- file it separately and in your own name;
- present it to the appellate authority, and send a copy to the authority that made the order;
- include all material statements and arguments you rely on;
- avoid disrespectful or improper language;
- make it complete in itself.

The authority that made the order must forward your appeal, its comments and the records to the appellate authority without avoidable delay [(Rule 26(3), PDF p. 29)](https://dopt.gov.in/sites/default/files/CCS-CCA-Rules-FINAL.pdf#page=29).
